  (text "NOTES\nJ1: battery / 12 V adapter wires soldered directly, zip-tie holes; 6-17 V\nD1: bidirectional: survives reversed battery\nR19: RC damper for hot-plug ringing: 0.47R + 2x10uF keeps a 16.8 V plug-in below OVP (sim S1)\nQ1: reverse-polarity blocking FET (TPS2663 datasheet Fig 9-2)\nQ2: B_GATE fast pull-down: Vds>=15V, Vgs max 20V, Ciss<=50pF, Vth(min)<=3V\nU1: MODE=GND auto-retry; SHDN floats (2.7 V open-circuit) = enabled; IMON unused\nR3: OVP 19.2 V typ (18.8-19.6), release >=17.44 V: full 4S 16.8 V never latches off (review P3)\nR5: I_OL = 18k/R = 5.0 A\nC3: 2.27 V/ms soft start\nC9: IN pins need >=0.1 uF (TPS2663 rec. operating)\nR8: LED fed from EF_IN: protected from reverse battery\nD2: eFuse fault LED (on = fault)\nR9: INA226 #1 shunt; route IN+/IN- as Kelvin traces from the pads\nU2: I2C 0x40 (A0=A1=GND): whole-node current + battery voltage\nR10: 1M/1M: 9 uA standby drain" (at 15 125.96 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 3be4a408-19a7-536e-90e6-e1583ba53045))
)
